{{Elections in Alabama sidebar}}
The '''2010 Alabama gubernatorial election''' took place on November 2, 2010. Incumbent Governor [[Bob Riley]] was term-limited and unable to seek re-election. The [[Partisan primary|party primaries]] were held on June 1, 2010,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.sos.state.al.us/elections/2010/ElectionInfo2010.aspx |title=Alabama Secretary of State's website |publisher=Sos.state.al.us |access-date=2010-06-06 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100527161857/http://www.sos.state.al.us/Elections/2010/ElectionInfo2010.aspx |archive-date=27 May 2010 |url-status=dead }}</ref> with a Republican [[runoff election|runoff]] on July 13. In the general election, [[Robert J. Bentley]] defeated Democrat [[Ron Sparks (politician)|Ron Sparks]]. This was the first election in which Republicans won three consecutive gubernatorial elections in the state. This was also the first time since Reconstruction that a Republican carried [[Colbert County, Alabama|Colbert County]], [[Franklin County, Alabama|Franklin County]], and [[Lawrence County, Alabama|Lawrence County]] in a gubernatorial race.

