*[[Bradley Byrne]], former state two-year college [[chancellor]], former [[Alabama Senate|state senator]] and former member of the [[Alabama State Board of Education]]<ref>{{cite web|author=File photo |url=http://blog.al.com/spotnews/2009/05/bradley_byrne_announces_run_fo.html |title=Bradley Byrne announces run for governor of Alabama &#124; al.com |publisher=Blog.al.com |date=2009-05-27 |access-date=2010-06-06}}</ref>
*[[Tim James (Alabama politician)|Tim James]], businessman, son of former Governor [[Fob James]] and candidate for governor in [[2002 Alabama gubernatorial election|2002]]<ref name=komo>{{cite web|url=http://hosted.ap.org/dynamic/external/pre-election/profilesstates/AL.html|title=Alabama State Profile|access-date=April 18, 2009|publisher=[[KOMO-TV]]}}</ref>
* Bill Johnson, former director of the Alabama Department of Economic and Community Affairs and former [[Birmingham, Alabama|Birmingham]] city councilman<ref name=johnson>{{cite web|url=http://www.al.com/news/birminghamnews/statebriefs.ssf?/base/news/1246090530215450.xml&coll=2 |title=Former Birmingham City Councilman Bill Johnson enters Alabama governor's race |publisher=The Birmingham News |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091129064401/http://www.al.com/news/birminghamnews/statebriefs.ssf?%2Fbase%2Fnews%2F1246090530215450.xml&coll=2 |archive-date=2009-11-29 }}</ref>
*[[Roy Moore]], former [[Alabama Supreme Court|chief justice of the Alabama Supreme Court]] and candidate for governor in [[2006 Alabama gubernatorial election|2006]]<ref>{{cite web|author=Screen reproduction |url=http://blog.al.com/spotnews/2009/06/roy_moore_makes_it_official_he.html |title=Roy Moore makes it official, he's running for Alabama governor &#124; al.com |publisher=Blog.al.com |date=2009-06-01 |access-date=2010-06-06}}</ref>
